@page "/data-deletion"
@{
  ViewData["Title"] = "Data Deletion — Queenzone";
  ViewData["Description"] = "How to request deletion of your personal data from Queenzone.";
  ViewData["CanonicalPath"] = "/data-deletion";
}

<partial name="_PageHero" model='@(("Your Data", "Data Deletion", "How to remove your personal information from Queenzone.", "Last updated 12 August 2026"))' />

<section class="qz-section qz-section--warm">
  <div class="qz-container qz-container--text">

    <p class="lede">You can delete your account and personal sign-in data at any time.</p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <p>If you have a Queenzone account, we store your email address, display name, and (where applicable) a reference to the social login provider you used (Google, Microsoft, Discord, or GitHub). We do not store passwords in plain text.</p>

    <h2>How to delete your account</h2>
    <p>Sign in, open <a href="/account/settings">Account settings</a>, and select <strong>Delete my account</strong>. You will be signed out after confirming the request.</p>
    <p>If you cannot sign in, email <a href="mailto:privacy@queenzone.org">privacy@queenzone.org</a> from the address associated with your account.</p>

    <h2>What happens after the request</h2>
    <p>Your public display name changes immediately to <strong>Deleted member</strong>. Your profile and avatar are hidden, and forum posts and private messages remain with anonymised attribution.</p>
    <p>During the <strong>30-day cooling-off period</strong>, you can sign back in and cancel deletion from Account settings. Cancelling restores your display name, avatar, profile, and retained-content attribution.</p>
    <p>After 30 days, sign-in is blocked and we permanently purge your email address, password hash, social sign-in references, and stored avatar. We retain a non-personal account record so content relationships remain valid. Any existing link to a legacy QueenZone account is retained for now.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For any questions about your data, email <a href="mailto:privacy@queenzone.org">privacy@queenzone.org</a>.</p>

  </div>
</section>
